\documentclass{report}
\title{Lifelong SLAM for Warehouse Mobile Robots}
\author{R. Echeverria}
\date{July 2026}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\input{chapters/intro}
\input{chapters/methods}
\input{chapters/results}
\end{document}

\chapter{Results}
The system ran continuously for eleven weeks in a working warehouse.
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{lll}
\hline
Policy & Localisation error (cm) & Map size \\
\hline
Frozen map & 8.1 & 1.0 GB \\
Naive update & 5.4 & 3.7 GB \\
Consensus update & 4.2 & 1.6 GB & yes \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}
The consensus policy halves the localisation error of the frozen map
while keeping the map size close to that of the initial build.

